WEBVTT

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:34.010
Yum!

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:39.030
It's been a while since I had 
a sweet, jaw-dropping crepe.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.430
Hinata, you've got cream on your cheek.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:42.180
Really?

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.060
No, the other side.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:47.120
Did I get it?

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:47.980
Yeah.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.610
It's because you're careless, Hinata.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.340
That's not true!

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:53.790
Yes, it is.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:54.810
Know what?

00:01:54.810 --> 00:02:00.440
As a kid, Hinata was the type who'd fall 
into ditches and plunge into rivers on her bike!

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:02.760
Was she really?

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:03.970
Come on!

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.680
Forget about the past.

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:07.070
No, I can't!

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:09.520
Not when it kept involving me too!

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.580
My...

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.040
Oh, I guess that did happen.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.110
That was really, really embarrassing!

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.900
It wasn't the end of the world!{this line gets repeated two more times, so needs to work}

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.740
That's not the issue!

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.490
Mountain Trail

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.410
Season 2 - New Climb 5

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.750
Season 2 - New Climb 5
 I Won't Forgive You!

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.000
Oh, say, Kokona-chan,

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.900
I'll be done with that thing soon.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.010
I can't wait!

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.500
What? What's this about?

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.550
Something none of your business!

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.430
Aw, come on!

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.220
Well, see you later, Kokona-chan.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.770
Goodbye!

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:48.600
Later!

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:55.790
Ow!

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.930
Aren't those polka dots?

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.430
Yeah, they're polka dots.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.030
Polka dots!

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.830
Hinata!

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:04.620
S-Sorry!

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.620
Well, it's not the end of the world.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.140
That's not the issue!

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.800
Aoi-san...

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.600
Oh, well...

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.380
I'd better apologize to her.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.530
Hey, Aoi!

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:21.630
Wait up!

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.810
Oh, welcome, Hinata-chan.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.810
Hello!

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.270
I wondered if Aoi might be home...

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.070
She is.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.820
Aoi! It's Hinata-chan!

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.360
Come on, it wasn't on purpose. 
And I said I was sorry!

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.030
Okay, fine...

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:50.460
You can pull down my skirt! 
Then we'll be even!

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:53.250
Go ahead!

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.220
We don't need to do that, silly!

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:00.880
I'm sorry.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.410
It's fine.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:07.010
But, you really are just as careless 
as you were back then, Hinata.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.990
That's not true!

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.530
I'm in high school now!

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:13.390
I'm a mature adult woman!

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.460
In what way?

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.790
Aoi!

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.900
I have drinks, so come get them!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.270
Coming!

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.970
Wait just a moment.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.120
Even more handmade stuff?

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.980
She's pretty good!

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.790
What's this, a knit hat?

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.000
Huh, that'll look kinda cute.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.660
How you work these things, anyway?

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.560
Hinata, I'm ba—

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.850
I-I was just, uh...

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.400
...practicing drumming!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.570
Hinata!

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:07.810
Sorry!

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:09.830
I was gonna fix it, honest!

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.680
You're too clumsy and 
careless to ever do that!

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.740
You didn't have to put it that way.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.430
Can't you just reknit it?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.600
Um...

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:23.600
Go away.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:25.630
Aoi?

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:26.670
Go away!

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.890
You lummox!{needs to be a word she might not recognize}

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:34.160
Aoi sure was mad.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:37.890
Well, she should be in 
a better mood tomorrow.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.350
What's a "lummox"?

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:45.570
Aoi, good morning!

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:49.360
Huh?

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.160
Hey, are you still mad?

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.170
Yamato Kingdom
Alliance Around 
One Royal Family{not sure about what to use for 'ouken', seems to mean 'royal power/right to rule', but here it's used more in a territory sense. using 'Kingdom' for now, but 'Dynasty', 'Kingship' and 'Sovereignty' are other possibilities}

00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:01.690
The regions of Kinai, northern Kanto, 
San-in, San-you, and northern Kyushu

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.960
formed the Yamato Kingdom.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.760
However, this is considered to have 
been more of an alliance than a nation.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.650
What the?

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:33.660
I see, so Aoi-san is upset.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.070
Sure, it was all my fault,

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:38.410
but she didn't have to get so mad.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.440
Aoi could easily knit another one, right?

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.760
Aw man, they aren't skipping at all.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.580
Um, Hinata-san...

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:53.100
I was keeping this a secret,

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.890
but that knit hat that you undid

00:06:56.890 --> 00:07:01.470
was being knitted by Aoi-san 
as a present for you.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:07.130
I knew about it because we 
went to buy yarn together.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.110
Hmm, maybe this color would be good...

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.830
Oh, but this one may be better!

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.930
Wouldn't it look good on Hinata?

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.930
Yes, it's a very nice color.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.500
I'm sure it will look great on her.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.510
As thanks for showing me Mt. Fuji last time,

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:25.010
next time I'll have a surprise for her.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:28.060
I hope Hinata-san likes it.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:28.900
Yeah!

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:33.760
I hope she'll wear it 
while mountain climbing.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.430
She said happily that she would 
soon be done knitting it.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:43.140
I think Aoi-san got upset 
because that went to waste.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.210
So that's why.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:48.430
Aoi...

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.610
Say, Kokona-chan,

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:54.600
would you teach me?

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:56.660
Yes, I'd love to!

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:01.060
This is how you do it.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:05.360
Wow!

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.330
Using a nice wrist snap,

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:08.230
aim at the surf—

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:12.340
No, I didn't mean for you to 
teach me how to skip stones.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:19.680
Pleasant Mountain Hiking

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.440
Stupid Hinata...

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:41.450
<i>I still haven't spoken to Hinata since then.</i>

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.580
Hinata

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.580
<i>But then, she hasn't spoken to me either.</i>

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:53.070
<i>Though I'm not even mad at her anymore, 
I never have a chance to talk to her.</i>

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:04.890
Yukimura

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:04.890
<i>Coming!</i>

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.390
Aoi! It's Hinata-chan!

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:15.400
What do you want?

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.660
Nothing in particular, but, uh...

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.190
Aoi...

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.330
Here.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.080
What's that?

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.170
Kokona-chan told me about 
the hat you were knitting.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:37.120
Knowing I'd done something terrible,

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:39.950
I thought I'd knit one for you,

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.940
so I asked Kokona-chan how to knit...

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.850
but my progress was slow.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:49.070
<i>So that's why she was sleeping in class,</i>

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.710
<i>and leaving right after school.</i>

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:56.980
But, this doesn't look like a knit hat.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.930
Since it won't be ready in 
time for winter at this rate,

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:02.160
here's what I have.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:05.080
You could use it as a coaster... maybe?

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:11.480
You managed to knit very 
neatly partway through,

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.290
but the rest got messy.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:17.420
The neat part is where 
Kokona-chan helped me out.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:22.490
The part she helped with 
is much bigger, isn't it?

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.310
Hey, it's because I'd never done it before!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.460
It's really because you're clumsy, Hinata.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:30.400
Still, thank you.

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:32.610
I'm sorry!

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:35.720
No, I got more upset than I should've.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:37.970
I'll treasure this and use it.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:38.740
Sure!

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:42.500
<i>Though we can't help 
arguing from time to time,</i>

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.800
<i>we need to make up quickly!</i>

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.780
<i>Instead of getting all stubborn,</i>

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:50.960
<i>we should be a bit more honest 
and forgiving of each other.</i>

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:58.710
So, Aoi, when will you finish 
knitting that hat for me?

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:01.190
Huh? I'm not knitting it anymore.

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:03.000
But why not?!

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.260
Isn't it a surprise present for me?

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:07.770
If you know, then it's not a surprise!

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:11.320
Come on, say something, Kokona-chan!

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:14.600
Certainly! This ice cream is delicious.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:15.860
That's not what I meant!

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:19.110
It's been a while since 
I had soft-serve ice cream.

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.870
Well, see you later, Kokona-chan.{match earlier}

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.290
Goodbye!{match earlier}

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.490
Later!{match earlier}

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.290
Ow!{match earlier}

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:32.580
Aren't those teddy bears?{match earlier style}

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:33.900
Yeah, they're teddy bears.{match earlier style}

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.210
Teddy bears!{match earlier style}

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:37.960
Aoi!

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.350
Sorry!

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:41.470
But it's not the end of the world.{mostly match earlier}

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:45.010
Besides, you told me to pull 
down your skirt earlier, right?

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.010
Right?

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.760
That was clearly a joke!

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:50.900
Okay, <i>now</i> we're even!

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.390
You call this even?! Wait up!

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:55.510
How could you do that to me?!{semi-ad-lib}

00:11:55.510 --> 00:11:57.740
Eek! I'm so scared!{ad-lib?}

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.980
To Be Continued!
